From: mrdidit <26687854+mrdidit@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: Subscribe to encoder output picture type

The Gen2 response handler uses HFI_PROP_PICTURE_TYPE to assign the V4L2
KEYFRAME, PFRAME and BFRAME buffer flags. Encoder sessions currently skip
all property subscriptions, although consumers need these flags to
recognize an independently decodable start to the stream.

Request picture-type metadata for the encoder bitstream port through the
existing subscription path. Leave raw-input and decoder subscriptions
unchanged. The working Frame vendor driver independently subscribes to
the same property on its encoder output port.

On KPFE, the baseline 90-frame H.264 encode contained three IDR frames
and 87 P frames but exported no KEYFRAME or PFRAME flags. The patched
Linux 7.2.6 test image reported all 90 frame types correctly and produced
byte-identical H.264 output. Steam recordings on that image, together
with the force-keyframe backport, saved visible video and audio; both
short clips passed complete decoding and timestamp checks. Several
additional recordings completed successfully. Overall stability remains under
investigation following a hard freeze with uncertain timing outside
active recording.

---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
@@ -1052,6 +1052,7 @@
 
 static int iris_hfi_gen2_subscribe_property(struct iris_inst *inst, u32 plane)
 {
+	static const u32 enc_output_properties[] = { HFI_PROP_PICTURE_TYPE };
 	struct iris_core *core = inst->core;
 	u32 subscribe_prop_size = 0, i;
 	const u32 *subcribe_prop = NULL;
@@ -1059,10 +1060,13 @@
 
 	payload[0] = HFI_MODE_PROPERTY;
 
-	if (inst->domain == ENCODER)
-		return 0;
-
-	if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(plane)) {
+	if (inst->domain == ENCODER) {
+		if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(plane))
+			return 0;
+
+		subcribe_prop = enc_output_properties;
+		subscribe_prop_size = ARRAY_SIZE(enc_output_properties);
+	} else if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(plane)) {
 		subscribe_prop_size = core->iris_firmware_data->dec_input_prop_size;
 		subcribe_prop = core->iris_firmware_data->dec_input_prop;
 	} else {
